<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Campeche</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Campeche is a state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> on the western side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán Peninsula</a>, facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>. Its interior holds major Maya sites such as Calakmul and Edzná, and its capital, the walled colonial port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco-de-campeche">San Francisco de Campeche</a>, gave the state its name. It was separated from Yucatán in 1857 and recognised as a state in 1863.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/campeche.jpg" alt="Campeche" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (WT-en) Lahoriali at English Wikivoyage · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calakmul_bio_reserve.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
